"# Terms of Service\n\nLast updated: September 8, 2026\n\n## 1. Provider and agreement\n\nSocialMint is operated by productivity-boost.com Betriebs UG (haftungsbeschränkt) & Co. KG, Reichenbergerstr. 2, 94036 Passau, Germany (\"we\" or \"us\"). Contact: [info@productivity-boost.com](mailto:info@productivity-boost.com). Company representation and registration details appear in our [Impressum](/impressum).\n\nThese terms govern your SocialMint account and subscription. You must have authority to act for any organization you register. Keep account details accurate and credentials private. SocialMint is intended for agencies and freelancers using it professionally.\n\n## 2. Service and plans\n\nSocialMint is a hosted subscription service for preparing and scheduling social posts across brands and following publishing results. Agency also provides client approval links, API access, and an n8n node.\n\n- Starter: €19 per month, up to 3 brands and 1 user.\n- Agency: €49 per month, up to 15 brands and 5 users. Client reviewers using approval links do not consume team seats.\n\nPrices include applicable VAT. Checkout shows the total recurring amount before an order is placed.\n\nSupported launch networks are X, Bluesky, Mastodon, Telegram, and Threads. LinkedIn, Instagram, and Facebook are planned but unavailable pending platform approvals. No release dates are promised. Networks control their own permissions, limits, and availability; their rules also apply to your use.\n\n## 3. Free trial and paid subscriptions\n\nThe trial lasts 14 days and requires no payment card. It provides the chosen plan's stated limits. A paid subscription begins only after you expressly select it and complete checkout. The trial does not automatically turn into a paid subscription. Without a paid subscription, publishing stops at trial end.\n\nPaid subscriptions are billed monthly in advance through Stripe and renew for successive monthly billing periods until canceled. The checkout displays your plan, recurring price, and billing terms before payment. Your customer portal shows the next renewal date.\n\n## 4. Cancellation, failed payments, and refunds\n\nYou may cancel anytime in the customer portal. Cancellation stops the next renewal; access continues until the end of the current paid billing period. There is no additional cancellation fee. If you cannot access the portal, contact us for help with cancellation.\n\nWe do not provide prorated refunds for unused portions of a billing period, except where required by law. Statutory refund, withdrawal, defect, and extraordinary termination rights remain unaffected. Where a refund is due, we return it through the original payment method where possible.\n\nIf payment fails, we notify you and give a reasonable opportunity to resolve it before suspending paid access, unless immediate action is legally necessary. Posts cannot be published through a suspended or expired subscription. Cancellation is separate from account deletion; retention is explained in our Privacy Policy.\n\n## Consumer right of withdrawal\n\nOur offer is primarily intended for businesses. If you subscribe as a consumer, you have the right to withdraw from the contract within 14 days of its conclusion without giving a reason. The free trial does not replace this statutory right.\n\nTo exercise your right, send an unequivocal statement to productivity-boost.com Betriebs UG (haftungsbeschränkt) & Co. KG, Reichenbergerstr. 2, 94036 Passau, Germany, email info@productivity-boost.com, telephone +49 178 1981631. Sending the notice before the deadline is sufficient. You may use the model form below, but it is not mandatory.\n\nIf you withdraw, we reimburse payments received without undue delay and no later than 14 days after receiving your notice, using the original payment method unless expressly agreed otherwise, without reimbursement fees. If you expressly requested the service to begin during the withdrawal period, you must pay a proportionate amount for the service provided up to your withdrawal. The right expires upon full performance only if the legal requirements, including your prior express consent and acknowledgment, are met.\n\n### Model withdrawal form\n\nTo: productivity-boost.com Betriebs UG (haftungsbeschränkt) & Co. KG, Reichenbergerstr. 2, 94036 Passau, Germany; info@productivity-boost.com.\n\nI/We hereby withdraw from my/our contract for the provision of the following service: SocialMint subscription.\n\nOrdered on: __________. Name of consumer(s): __________. Address of consumer(s): __________. Date: __________. Signature of consumer(s), only if submitted on paper: __________.\n\n## 5. Your content and acceptable use\n\nYou retain ownership of your content. You grant us the limited permission needed to store, process, display to your authorized reviewers, and transmit it to the networks you select, solely to provide the service. This includes using our service providers for those purposes.\n\nYou are responsible for your content, required permissions, account connections, publishing instructions, and compliance with applicable law and network rules. Client approval does not establish copyright ownership or legal compliance. Protect approval links and API credentials and notify us if access is compromised.\n\nDo not use SocialMint for spam, unlawful content, impersonation, infringement, harassment, platform-rule violations, or attempts to bypass access controls or rate limits. Do not disrupt our service or other users. We may restrict access proportionately to address a breach, security threat, or legal requirement. Where feasible, we explain the reason and allow you to remedy the issue; urgent threats may require immediate suspension. Either party retains statutory rights to terminate for serious cause.\n\n## 6. Publishing and availability\n\nWe operate the service with reasonable care on a best-effort basis. No specific uptime percentage or service-level agreement is included. Maintenance, faults, network outages, revoked permissions, and third-party restrictions may delay or prevent publication.\n\nWe show publishing status, errors, and retry activity. Some failures can be retried; others require your action. Scheduling or approving a post is not a guarantee that a network will publish it at an exact time. Monitor posts that are time-sensitive. This section does not remove our contractual duties or statutory remedies.\n\n## 7. Liability\n\nWe are liable without limitation for intent, gross negligence, injury to life, body, or health, and liability that cannot lawfully be limited, including under the German Product Liability Act and for guarantees expressly assumed.\n\nFor ordinary negligence, we are liable for breach of an essential contractual obligation on which you may normally rely to receive the service. That liability is limited to foreseeable damage typical of this type of contract. Otherwise, liability for ordinary negligence is excluded to the extent permitted by law. These limits also apply to our representatives and persons performing our obligations. They do not restrict mandatory rights under data protection law.\n\n## 8. Privacy and customer data\n\nOur [Privacy Policy](/privacy) explains personal-data processing, recipients, retention, and your rights. Where we process personal data on your instructions, a separate data processing agreement applies. You are responsible for a lawful basis and required notices for client content and reviewer data you provide.\n\n## 9. Changes\n\nWe may improve the service without materially reducing the agreed subscription. Material changes to prices, core features, or these terms require a lawful basis and any consent required by law. We will explain proposed material changes and their effective date by email at least 30 days in advance. We do not treat silence alone as acceptance of a contractual amendment. If we cannot continue the existing contract without an agreed change, we may end it through lawful